    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "Lack of access control. Lost: ~$180k"
    },
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "Because of a lack of Access control over specific functions 0x7ca06d68 , Attacker can manipulate the _uniswapV3MintCallback value and execute the attack contract directly. Code Snippet: Attack Tx: https://etherscan.io/tx/0x93a033917fcdbd5fe8ae24e9fe22f002949cba2f621a1c43a54f6519479caceb https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/eth/0x93a033917fcdbd5fe8ae24e9fe22f002949cba2f621a1c43a54f6519479caceb Analysis: https://blog.solidityscan.com/civnft-hack-analysis-4ee79b8c33d1"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "CIVNFT suffered a smart contract exploit on Ethereum Mainnet on July 8, 2023, after deploying a function with no access control that allowed arbitrary token transfers. The attacker used this flaw to steal over $180,000 in tokens. A privileged contract function (0x7ca06d68) in CIVNFT lacked access control, enabling any address to trigger fund transfers, resulting in theft."
    }
  ],
